# PSR-6c — Harbor persistent catalog inventory

## Context

After **PSR-6b** Harbor is `stub` (option A). Durable G1 still blocked by:

1. Default HTTP → `501 WORKSPACE_GUEST_STUB` unless `HARBOR_SMOKE_E2E_SEED=1`
2. `HarborSmokeCatalogStore` — process-memory Map
3. No product HTTP host / tour-store / RLS request context (unlike Denali/Urban)

Portal intake already POSTs upstream `/harbor/registrations` (see
`catalog-intake.ts`); marketing browse hits `/harbor/catalog*`. Both land on
the **same smoke handlers** — fixing the Harbor HTTP surface fixes portal +
marketing.

## Current call graph

```text
marketing  → GET  /harbor/catalog[/:id]  → harbor-catalog-http (smoke factory)
portal     → POST /api/catalog/registrations
           → buildUpstreamRequest path=/harbor/registrations
           → harbor-catalog-http (smoke factory)
smoke factory → isSeedEnabled? else 501
             → HarborSmokeCatalogStore (memory) when seed on
```

Denali reference (do **not** clone):

```text
GET /denali/catalog* → product.routes → catalog.service
  → host.resolveTourStore + runWithHttpRequestContext (RLS)
POST /denali/registrations → registration.service + idempotency/capacity
configure-product-http-hosts.ts wires Denali/Urban hosts only — Harbor absent
```

## Target architecture (approved direction)

| Layer | Decision |
| --- | --- |
| Product package | Keep Harbor **thin**; map published tours → Harbor Event card; city filter stays product-owned |
| Host wiring | Add Harbor (or shared G1) product HTTP host configured from `apps/api` like Denali/Urban — **no** branded import in configure body beyond generated façade |
| Data | Reuse platform `resolveProductTourStore` + existing registration persistence (capacity/idempotency ports) under tenant RLS |
| Smoke seed | `HARBOR_SMOKE_E2E_SEED` becomes **dev/e2e seed-only** (ensure fixture tour rows), not the sole production gate |
| Default path | Production/prodlike: durable port enabled; missing published tours → empty list / 404, **not** 501 stub |
| SDK | Evolve `WorkspaceGuestSmokeCatalogPort` toward async + optional `isDurableEnabled` **or** replace Harbor handlers with host-bound routes using neutral SDK catalog helpers (`filterWorkspacePublishedTours`, `loadWorkspaceTourIfPublished`, …) |

## Explicit forbidden moves

- Copying `denali/.../catalog.service.ts` / Denali exposure stack into Harbor
- Keeping `certified` until durable default path + proofs exist (already demoted)
- File/sqlite “fake durable” store as production SoT
- Full `phase-*:gate` without Architect YES

## Proposed sub-slices (after this inventory)

| Slice | Scope | Risk |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **PSR-6c1** | SDK: async catalog/registration port + factory path that can skip 501 when durable mode on | med |
| **PSR-6c2** | Harbor thin host + card mapper from published tour; keep city filter | med |
| **PSR-6c3** | API: generated host binding + `configure*` for Harbor tour store + registration adapters | high |
| **PSR-6c4** | Seed helper writes/reads real store for e2e; default path non-501 | med |
| **PSR-6c5** | Restart/idempotency/RLS proofs + CERT rebind path (ties PSR-5i live) | high |

This wave ships **inventory + smoke only** — no handler/host mutate.

## Smoke

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-6c-harbor-persistent-catalog-smoke.mjs
```

## Residual

- PSR-5i live same-SHA pack still needs Architect YES
- Recert / `productionTier: certified` only after 6c4–6c5
